---
import Callout from "~/components/illustration-kit/Callout.astro"
import IllustrationFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/IllustrationFigure.astro"
import Panel from "~/components/illustration-kit/Panel.astro"

const opening = ["H", "H", "H"]
const later = ["H", "H", "T", "H", "H", "H"]
---

<IllustrationFigure lead="How can THH beat HHH, even though both have a 1 in 8 chance in three tosses?">
  <p class="text-base leading-normal">
    The first player chooses <strong>HHH</strong>. The second chooses <strong>THH</strong>. H
    means heads; T means tails. There are two ways the race can unfold.
  </p>

  <Panel title="1. The exception: HHH wins immediately">
    <div class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-6 gap-1 text-center sm:gap-2">
      {opening.map((toss, index) => (
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1">
          <span class="text-xs sm:text-sm">Toss {index + 1}</span>
          <span class="flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 border-series-red text-base font-bold sm:h-11 sm:w-11">
            {toss}
          </span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-normal">
      <strong>HHH wins on tosses 1–3.</strong> This is the only way HHH can win the race. It
      happens 1 time in 8.
    </p>
  </Panel>

  <Panel title="2. Otherwise: the game is already underway">
    <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-normal">
      In this example, the first two tosses are HH, but the third is T. Now watch what happens
      when heads start appearing again.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-2">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-6 gap-1 text-center sm:gap-2">
        {later.map((toss, index) => (
          <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1">
            <span class="text-xs sm:text-sm">{index === 5 ? "6*" : index + 1}</span>
            <span
              class:list={[
                "flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 text-base font-bold sm:h-11 sm:w-11",
                index === 5 ? "border-dashed border-ink" : "border-ink",
              ]}
            >
              {toss}
            </span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-6 gap-1 sm:gap-2">
        <span class="col-span-3 col-start-3 border-t-4 border-series-blue pt-1 text-center font-bold">
          THH wins
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-6 gap-1 sm:gap-2">
        <span class="col-span-3 col-start-4 border-t-4 border-series-red pt-1 text-center font-bold">
          HHH too late
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-normal">
      <strong>THH appears in tosses 3–5.</strong> HHH would appear in tosses 4–6, one toss
      later. The sixth toss (*) is hypothetical: the game ends at toss 5.
    </p>
  </Panel>

  <Callout tone="accent">
    <p class="leading-normal">
      <strong>Why this always happens after the opening:</strong> If HHH appears later for the
      first time, the toss just before it must be T. If it were H, HHH would have appeared one
      toss earlier. That T followed by the first two heads makes THH win before HHH can finish.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <Fragment slot="caption">
    HHH can win only on the first three tosses, with a 1 in 8 chance. In all other cases, THH
    wins first, with a 7 in 8 chance. Equal odds for a fixed set of three tosses do not mean
    equal odds of appearing first in a running game.
  </Fragment>
</IllustrationFigure>
